Apple today shared a short video featuring an Apple Watch user named Amanda who says her device saved her life.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Apple Watch Heart Rate: Amanda's True Apple Watch Story" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/TVpTonS1QVw" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
In 2024, Amanda began receiving alerts about an abnormal heart rate. Her watch alerted her about changes to her resting heart rate and her overnight vitals, prompting her to visit her doctor.<br/>
<br/>
She ended up being diagnosed with acute myeloid leukemia, an aggressive cancer. After treatment, she is in remission.<br/>
<br/>
"I absolutely believe that if it wasn't for my Apple Watch, I wouldn't be talking to you," she said.<br/>
<br/>
